    "result_text": "Done. The full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required a read-only `checkDigit` field on an owner = a single Luhn check digit computed over the digits of the owner's `customerCode`.\n\nTwo changes, following the project's existing patterns for derived Owner fields:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `checkDigit` property to the `Owner` schema (integer 0\u20139, `readOnly`), placed right after `customerCode`. The DTO (`OwnerDto`) is generated from this spec at build time.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping(target = \"checkDigit\", ... qualifiedByName = \"formatCheckDigit\")` and a `formatCheckDigit(Owner)` method that runs the standard Luhn algorithm over the digit characters of `customerCode` (skipping non-digits like the `TOW-SUR-0001` letters/hyphens), returning `null` when the code is absent. This mirrors how `membershipNumber`, `membershipLevel`, etc. are derived.\n\nThe `AcceptanceTest.coreCheckDigitIsLuhnOfCustomerCode` test recomputes Luhn from the returned `customerCode` and asserts the exact returned `checkDigit` \u2014 it now passes.",
