    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change follows the established pattern in this mapper exactly. `OwnerMapper` already derives several read-only DTO fields via `@Named(\"formatX\")` default methods (`formatLocality`, `formatMembershipLevel`, `formatMembershipNumber`), and `formatCheckDigit` slots in identically:\n\n- It's placed among the other `format*` derivation methods, right after `formatMembershipNumber`, mirroring the `@Mapping` order at the top.\n- Inline derivation logic of this size is already the norm here \u2014 `formatLocality` (~15 lines) and `formatMembershipLevel` (~14 lines) carry comparable self-contained logic in the interface rather than in a helper, so keeping the Luhn computation inline is consistent rather than a new catch-all.\n- The null-guard (`owner == null || getCustomerCode() == null`), `Integer` return type, and Javadoc style match the neighbouring methods.\n- No duplication, and the OpenAPI schema addition is a clean, parallel `readOnly` field definition.\n\nOne could imagine extracting the Luhn routine into a small utility class alongside `AddressNormalizer`/`TelephoneNormalizer`, but those utilities exist because their logic is shared with the persistence/validation path; `checkDigit` is a purely local derivation used only here, so inlining it matches the `format*` methods rather than the `normalize*` ones. The structure is coherent and a maintainer would find it natural.",
